# A scraper's own output is large, machine-specific and stale by the time
# anyone reads it. The two committed samples are the exception.
*.json
*.csv
!sample_output.json
!sample_output.csv
flippa_listings.*
*.meta.json
*_debug.html
*_debug.png
# --dump-html X over several pages writes X.page2, X.page3 …, which no
# suffix rule above covers (family template §26).
*.page[0-9]*

# ANY working directory a live run writes into, not one chosen name: a
# sibling committed a 1.5 MB raw dump through `live/` because only
# `live_results/` was listed (family template §24).
live/
live_results/
out/
output/
runs/
results/
tmp/
scratch/
dumps/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.fingerprint_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
*.key
secrets*

# Local-only working directories, announced here rather than hidden in
# .git/info/exclude — that file is not cloned, so every fresh checkout used to
# start with no rule against committing these.
#   captures/  multi-megabyte page dumps the fixtures were cut from
#   legacy/    the superseded first version of this scraper, kept for reference
captures/
legacy/

# Every spelling of a working .env, not just `.env`: a `.env.bak` or
# `.env.local` is exactly how a live key gets one `git add -A` from a commit
# (family template §22). The negation keeps the documented example tracked.
.env*
!.env.example
